WEBVTT

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.400
Don't complain

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:10.280
We departed from the island where we had made so many memories.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:15.560
With the Orion aimed at the as-yet unseen mainland, our voyage continued.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:18.600
Hey, Luna!

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.630
Come get food!

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.900
Okay!

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.990
Here. It's breakfast.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:27.600
Thank you.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:32.810
Yum.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.350
Menori, you hafta eat properly.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.490
I'll have it later.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.630
Not feeling well, Menori?

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.260
No.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:44.700
I'm fine.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.210
Really? Well, you're off shift in a lil' while.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.230
We're counting on you.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.480
Keep it up!

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:51.750
Okay.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.100
Hey, Howard...

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.030
Sorry, but can you keep lookout next?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.310
It's Shingo's turn, but...

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:12.490
No helpin' it. Shingo 'n Adam're totally down with seasickness.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:17.440
We ought to cover their shifts for a little while.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:21.300
Honestly! What a pitiful pair they are!

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.830
Getting seasick even though it's so calm.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:28.460
If you take the sea lightly, you're in for a grim fate.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:34.010
Don't say such creepy things, Kaoru.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.110
Howard, please.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:38.210
Okay.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.290
He sure can put it away.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.900
It's 'cuz he's a growin' boy.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.800
But anyways, it's blue far's the eye can see in the middle of the sea.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:14.870
Kaoru...

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:15.900
How're they doin'?

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.780
There's nothing we can do for them.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:23.060
Adam...

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.450
I don't feel good.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.240
Have you gotten any better?

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.610
I keep feeling worse and worse.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.500
They ain't eatin' anythin' like this.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:40.690
If they don't eat, they won't have any strength.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:42.750
All they can do for now is sleep.

00:04:43.460 --> 00:04:46.010
When it's your turn to rest, you should rest too, Kaoru.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:46.800
Yeah.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:48.600
Luna, let's go.

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.350
Adam, Shingo, I'll come back later.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.730
I'm delighted, Luna.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:13.130
It's a cute embroidery.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:22.010
Even though you've come so far, your dad's backpack came along too.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:27.000
I'll keep it with me from now on, too. Right?

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:29.030
Yeah, you bet.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.150
This will do nicely.

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:37.990
Shift change.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.230
Nice work.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.760
Yeah, please do.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.250
Menori!

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.260
You okay?

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.510
I'm just a little tired.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.780
I'll be fine once I get a little fresh air.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:55.090
Later.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:57.900
Have a good rest.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.710
I give up! Yeesh.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.000
What a pain!

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.240
Howard, what's wrong?

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:17.780
I'm sick of this.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:24.340
You have to keep watch properly.

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.680
It's not like there's any ship but ours.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.850
That's true.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.810
After getting pounded on by the sun up there, I'm about to fall over.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:49.840
Want some?

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:51.790
I'm fine.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.390
I wonder if the mainland is even out there.

00:07:00.260 --> 00:07:02.510
There's less wind'n we thought.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:09.300
At this speed, the soonest we can reach the mainland's three or four days later'n expected.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.840
Three or four days...

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:17.210
We don't need to worry since we brought extra food and drinking water...

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.180
...but the problem is everyone's strength.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:26.290
Isn't there a way we can arrive even a little sooner?

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.980
Nothin' we can do.

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:30.680
We can't go any faster'n this.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:31.840
It's true.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.940
It'd be nice if a strong wind'd come blowin' in, though...

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:38.850
As if!

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.290
Menori...

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.240
It's time for our shift.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.300
Yeah...

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:12.340
Menori!

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:19.240
What's wrong?

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.990
I'm, er, I'm fine.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.140
I'll be right there.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.230
Don't push yourself.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:28.910
Rest up!

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:41.850
What?

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.530
Howard, Sharla, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.660
It's time for a shift change.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:08:59.930
Are you okay?

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.950
Nope.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.510
I feel awful, Luna.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.140
Sharla...

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.530
Are you okay?

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:22.050
For the meantime, I've switched it over to autopilot.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.510
So the only ones up 'n about are us.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:31.580
We'll just have to get by with just us somehow.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:36.980
No more! Let me off!

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:39.790
I'm at my limit too...

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.150
It hurts...

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:47.140
Whatever you say, but there's no island near here.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:49.800
There's nothin' we can do 'til we reach the mainland.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.200
Can't we just go back to the island?

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.890
Goin' back won't help anythin' either!

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:03.900
If I'd known it would be this way, I'd rather we didn't try to go to the mainland.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:05.250
Don't complain.

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.200
All we can do is tough it out.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:10.390
In two or three days, you'll all be better.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.900
I can't last that long!

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.790
Can't we go back to the island for now?

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:19.880
When we're over the seasickness, we can head out again.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.490
"Go back," you say...

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.450
It'll take another three days.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.890
You think it's just someone else's problem.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:28.910
I do not!

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:33.300
The one who said we'd go to the mainland in the first place was you, Luna.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:34.990
Take responsibility!

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.280
Responsibility?

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.660
Everyone agreed to it!

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:45.380
I said we should wait on the island for a rescue ship!

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:47.440
But Luna...

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:53.550
Maybe we should have considered other alternatives.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:56.810
What will saying that now accomplish?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:02.850
What's up with you? Always acting like you're so important. Who do you think you are?

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:05.250
Howard, stop it already.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:06.560
Luna!

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:10.990
You're the leader, right? Do something!

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:15.680
For now, we'll just continue like this.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:16.910
But...

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:19.010
...at this rate...

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:20.700
Luna...

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.240
I won't make it...

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:27.710
Whatever! Luna gets the last say anyways.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:31.760
Hey, whaddaya mean by that?

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:36.300
I know everyone is suffering...

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.040
...but I'm sorry. We can't go back to the island.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:46.280
Luna!

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:04.610
Everyone's saying things they don't mean because they're sick.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:11.850
I don't think it's your fault even a bit, Luna.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:14.890
Thanks.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.100
Just forget about it.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:21.980
The wind's gotten a little stronger. Put this on, just in case.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.210
You should rest a little as well.

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:32.550
Me? I'm fine!

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.390
Luna...

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:00.980
Okay! The wind's startin' to pick up!

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:01.990
Yeah.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.550
Now we can gain a little speed.

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:13.990
Luna...

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:15.790
Luna! Hurry down from there!

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.600
A storm?

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.380
A storm! A storm is coming!

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:34.010
Black clouds are headed this way!

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:36.640
Now the wind's blowin' too much!

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:39.860
How long will the gravity control unit hold out?

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.380
Luna!

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:05.210
Hurry down!

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:06.940
I have to get down...

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:14.850
Be careful.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.400
What?

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:36.150
A little further.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:43.540
Luna, are you okay?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.450
Let's furl the sail.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:49.580
Okay.

00:15:50.810 --> 00:15:51.680
Here we go!

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:10.690
One more time!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.550
Damn it!

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:18.450
We can't furl the sail because of the wind!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:27.260
Luna!

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:30.680
Are you okay?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:34.840
Oh no! We're gonna capsize!

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:37.950
Increasing output of Gyrostabilizer!

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:48.410
Are you okay?

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.450
What about your seasickness?

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.780
We just feel a little ill.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.280
We have to hurry and furl the sail.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.890
Alright, let's do it!

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:02.250
Heave-ho!

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:07.090
Damn it!

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:08.810
One more time!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.450
We're going to do it one more time!

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.510
One... two...

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:18.900
Three!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:42.410
Alright! One more time!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:48.150
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:53.810
Kaoru! At this rate, it'll overheat!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.040
What do we do?

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:05.060
To avoid capsizing, we'll turn off the gravity control unit and transfer its energy to the Gyrostabilizer!

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:06.750
That's all we can do.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.450
Gravity control unit: off!

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.350
Splashing down!

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:30.860
We should be okay now.

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:34.130
Okay!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:35.660
Everyone!

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:37.090
Sharla?

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:38.660
Hurry this way!

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:39.680
What's wrong?

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.060
The water...

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:50.850
Shingo!

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:57.380
Menori...

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.850
It's pointless unless we can plug this up!

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:06.080
We're counting on you.

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:38.810
This is all the Gyrostabilizer can handle!

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.990
Hold in there somehow!

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:45.530
Luna?

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:47.890
Luna!

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:49.350
Are you okay?

00:19:49.800 --> 00:19:50.810
Sorry.

00:19:51.110 --> 00:19:52.460
Luna, take a rest.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.530
That's right, leave it to us!

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:55.800
Let's continue.

00:20:07.880 --> 00:20:09.490
There we go!

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.040
Just a little more.

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:17.250
Once more!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.130
Right. Howard, here we go!

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:23.360
Everyone...

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:23.960
Here.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:24.790
There!

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.100
Here we go!

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:37.350
Luna?

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:38.700
I'm fine!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.140
Just a little more!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:56.740
I'm done!

00:20:57.560 --> 00:21:00.680
Now if we just get rid of this water, we should be fine.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.500
The worst is over.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:06.790
What a relief!

00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:11.780
What is it?

00:21:12.110 --> 00:21:15.450
Everyone, weren't you feeling sick?

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:17.850
Come to think of it...

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:19.580
You're right.

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:21.980
We're completely...

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:23.360
...better, it would seem.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:29.480
And I was so worried about you.

00:21:30.110 --> 00:21:31.760
But it is good to hear.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:45.600
Another big one's comin'!

00:21:46.540 --> 00:21:47.810
We'll go over it!

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:01.500
My backpack!

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:02.330
Luna!

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:03.150
Stop!

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:06.450
Thank goodness!

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.000
Luna!

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:21.040
Bell...

00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:27.380
Don't... let... go...

00:22:29.400 --> 00:22:30.980
I can't... anymore...

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:32.100
Luna...

00:22:39.530 --> 00:22:42.340
Luna!

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:45.710
Bell!

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:53.210
Luna!

00:23:04.010 --> 00:23:07.390
Luna, you can't! You can't die!

00:23:08.210 --> 00:23:12.860
When you were little, you promised your dad you'd make a world where people could live.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:17.140
So you can't die in a place like this!

00:23:18.080 --> 00:23:20.740
You definitely have to make it home alive!

00:23:21.300 --> 00:23:23.740
Good luck, Luna!

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:28.690
Next time: I won't give up!
